    "name": "Backrooms: Final Exam Part II",
    "steam_appid": 3801330,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i><strong>Backrooms: Final Exam Part II</strong></i> is a cooperative horror game for 1\u20134 players. Together or alone, you'll return to a place you were never meant to leave. The deeper you go, the more uncertain it becomes whether there was ever a way out.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Even more complicated!</strong> </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Scary atmosphere! </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- 1 to 4 player co-op </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Proximity voice chat </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Immersive AI </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Game Difficulties </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Stealth </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Large &amp; difficult map </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Primitive but challenging gameplay </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Important Notes</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is not a typical Backrooms game. It doesn\u2019t follow every detail from the online community. Instead, it offers a unique interpretation, integrating select elements in a fresh and atmospheric way. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game includes flickering lights and audiovisual effects that may affect sensitive players. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Built using the <strong>SNK V2 system</strong> \u2014 featuring an improved main menu, enhanced lobby, online server browser, difficulty selection, player sound system (with UI feedback and AI reaction), and a dynamic visibility system based on movement, posture, and flashlight use.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i><strong>Backrooms: Final Exam Part II</strong></i> is a cooperative horror game for 1\u20134 players. Together or alone, you'll return to a place you were never meant to leave. The deeper you go, the more uncertain it becomes whether there was ever a way out.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Even more complicated!</strong> </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Scary atmosphere! </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- 1 to 4 player co-op </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Proximity voice chat </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Immersive AI </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Game Difficulties </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Stealth </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Large &amp; difficult map </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Primitive but challenging gameplay </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Important Notes</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is not a typical Backrooms game. It doesn\u2019t follow every detail from the online community. Instead, it offers a unique interpretation, integrating select elements in a fresh and atmospheric way. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game includes flickering lights and audiovisual effects that may affect sensitive players. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Built using the <strong>SNK V2 system</strong> \u2014 featuring an improved main menu, enhanced lobby, online server browser, difficulty selection, player sound system (with UI feedback and AI reaction), and a dynamic visibility system based on movement, posture, and flashlight use.</p>",
